  "content": {
    "equation": "In general, the formulas used to populate the table are:\nDose = Weight * Weight-Based Dose\n• Dose is calculated in units that correspond to the Weight-Based Dose (eg, mg, g,\nmg/minute)\n• Weight is input in kg\n• Weight-Based Dose units are drug-specific\n• Weight-Based Dose units are drug-specific\nNote: A dosage range may be provided; each portion of the range is calculated using the\nabove formula. Some agents have fixed-dose recommendations which are not\naffected by the weight input by the user.\nVolume = Dose / Concentration\n• Volume is calculated in units that correspond to the Dose and Concentration\nWhen the dose is provided as a rate (eg, mcg/minute), the volume to be administered will\nalso be calculated as a rate according to the following formula:\nInfuse Rate = (Dose / Concentration) / Time\n• Infuse Rate is calculated in units that correspond to the Dose, Concentration,\nand Time of administration\nNote: A range of volumes or rates may be provided; each portion of the range is\ncalculated using the above formula(s).",
